    "narrative": "For the July 6th slate, **Tyler Freeman** stands out as our premier option with a 63.69 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against Lauer (5.28 xERA) provides the highest SP skill boost on the board, making him a locked-in start. **Gavin Sheets** follows closely behind at 58.96; despite a neutral park factor, the platoon advantage against Pfaadt and the protection of hitting in the cleanup spot make him a high-floor play. While **Yainer Diaz** (59.25) also ranks in the \"Strong\" tier, he faces a moderate test against Mikolas, though his raw talent keeps him comfortably in the lineup despite a sub-optimal spot in the seven-hole.\n\nStrategic optimization favored speed and situational utility today, leading to the decision to bench several peripheral options. The most difficult cut was **Geraldo Perdomo** (55.93); while he offers moderate stability, his score was capped by a difficult matchup against Buehler. We are managing the roster carefully with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** sidelined on the IL, alongside off-day constraints for **Cal Raleigh** and **Lawrence Butler**. With SB being our scarcest category, **Jung Hoo Lee** remains a critical start at 50.11; his ability to exploit Gausman's slow delivery provides a fractional but necessary boost to our stolen base potential. We remain cautious of **Bryson Stott**, whose score dropped to 46.33 due to a platoon disadvantage against Cameron and the pitcher's efficiency in controlling the running game, keeping his status as a \"Marginal\" play for today\u2019s contest.",
